h=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>CH<sub>3</sub> has +I effect so in N <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> C bond electron will move towards nitrogen, So electron density increase at nitrogen.\n<br><br>And alkayl group also has +I effect, so it will also increase electron density at nitrogen.\n<br><br>As electron density at nitrogen increases, so tendency to donate electron pair increases and basic nature also increases.\n<br><br>In those following,\n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/X9Hxskvh6QBC1am2W/vtoqmIiYzVT3f6HNHArLZWb83V8Uk/dd7yrsYrMvT2IWdaDONyQv/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 239 English Explanation 3\">\n<br><br>double bond has (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> I) effect, it will decrease the availability of lone pair electron at nitrogen but at (b) double bond is closer to nitrogen, so (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> I) effect will be more powerful than compound at (a), so (b) will be less basic nature.\n<br><br>So, the order of basicity,  c &gt; d &gt; a &gt; b"
